============================================================================================
  parsed 5000 training steps and 51 validation points

  1) WARMUP: lrm rises 0.03 -> 1.00 and first reaches 1.00 at step 39
     (--warmup-steps default is 40; base_train.py:370 returns (it+1)/warmup_iters).
     Train loss over warmup: 10.3975 -> 7.6338. No spike, no NaN.
  2) PLATEAU (constant LR): steps 39..1768, lrm pinned at 1.00.
  3) WARMDOWN: begins step 1768 (35% through), lrm 0.99 -> 0.05 linearly.
     val bpb across warmdown: 1.2928 -> 1.1638 (+0.1289), i.e. 6.4% of the total gain arrives in the final 65% of steps.

  4) TRAIN vs VALIDATION on one axis (train nats/token -> bpb using 4.8096 bytes/token):
       step  train loss  train bpb   val bpb      gap
          0     10.3975     3.1189    3.1936  -0.0748
       1000      4.3813     1.3142    1.3711  -0.0569
       2000      4.1405     1.2420    1.2779  -0.0360
       3000      3.9747     1.1923    1.2223  -0.0300
       4000      3.8059     1.1416    1.1858  -0.0442
       5000      3.7424     1.1226    1.1638  -0.0412
     gap trend: first=-0.0748 mid=-0.0451 last=-0.0412
     The gap stays NEGATIVE/near zero and does not widen -> validation is not being
     abandoned by training. (Train loss is a running average over fresh, never-repeated
     shards - epoch stayed 1 all run - so this is a fresh-data vs held-out comparison,
     not a memorization test. That is why the gap can be <= 0.)

  5) THROUGHPUT DRIFT: tok/sec first=13,737 median=33,224 min=13,737 max=47,272
     64 of 5000 steps (1.3%) ran below 80% of median.
     Wall time 41.6m; peak memory 11,716 MiB.
     -> the tail is real and asymmetric, so mean tok/sec OVERSTATES throughput.
        Any 'per minute' claim must use total wall time, never mean step time.

  6) SAMPLE EVIDENCE (pulled from the base_eval section of the same log):
     <|bos|>The capital of France is the capital of France. The capital of France is the capital of France. Th
     <|bos|>The chemical symbol of gold is the gold of the gold. The gold is the gold of the gold. The
     <|bos|>If yesterday was Friday, then tomorrow will be the first time to get to the end of the day. If you
     <|bos|>The opposite of hot is the same as hot is the same as hot is the same as hot is the
     -> 4/7 conditioned samples contain a verbatim repeated phrase.
     Unconditioned samples are locally fluent English with correct syntax and
     punctuation, but no factual grounding and no coherence past a sentence.
     That combination - local fluency, zero factual recall, degenerate loops under
     greedy decoding - is the signature of a model that has learned the token
     distribution but not yet the content. It corroborates UNDERFITTING and rules
     out instability (a diverged model emits noise, not grammatical English).
