============================================================================================
D. VERDICT AND THE CHEAPEST FALSIFIER
============================================================================================
  Evidence for UNDERFITTING (accepted):
    - tokens:scaling-params = 3.53 vs ~20 optimal -> 5.7x undertrained.
    - val bpb still falling at the end: last 500 steps 1.1721 -> 1.1638 (+0.0083), never flat.
    - epoch counter stayed at 1: the model never saw a token twice, so it cannot have
      memorized the training set.
  Evidence AGAINST overfitting: train-vs-val gap does not widen (part C4), and with
    one epoch over 82M fresh tokens there is no repetition to overfit to.
  Evidence AGAINST instability: no loss spike, no NaN, monotone val curve (True), lrm followed
    the schedule exactly.
  => DIAGNOSIS: UNDERFITTING / budget-limited. Not overfitting, not instability.

  CHEAPEST FALSIFIER (~11 min, one run, already in the catalog):
    w2-tokens-10000  = the identical config at 10,000 steps instead of 5,000.
    Prediction if the underfitting diagnosis is right: val bpb keeps falling well past
    1.1638, roughly along the power law fit by the 51 points already measured.
    FALSIFIED if doubling the token budget buys < 0.02 bpb, or if val bpb turns UP while
    train loss keeps falling - either outcome would mean the run is capacity- or
    data-limited rather than budget-limited, and the right next move would be a bigger
    model or better data rather than more steps.
    Note this falsifier is cheaper AND more decisive than a seed replicate, because the
    predicted effect (0.008+ bpb over the last 500 steps alone) is far larger
    than any plausible seed noise.

